The revised dated escrow approval and release export follows this priority schedule, with left-to-right posting order.

1 | funding < 0 or fee < 0 or net < 0 | ERROR {amount=0, pay_on=requested_on, final_payment=false}
2 | approved equals null | PENDING {amount=net, pay_on=requested_on, final_payment=false}
3 | approved equals false | empty
4 | requested_on <= due_on | HOLD {amount=net, pay_on=due_on, final_payment=false}
5 | review | BENEFICIARY {amount=net*(100-20)/100, pay_on=release_on, final_payment=true} -> AUDIT {amount=0, pay_on=requested_on, final_payment=false} -> RETAIN {amount=net*20/100, pay_on=due_on, final_payment=false}
6 | otherwise | BENEFICIARY {amount=net, pay_on=release_on, final_payment=true} -> FEE {amount=fee, pay_on=requested_on, final_payment=false}

net is funding less fee. Date comparisons use UTC timestamps. Each nonsilent contract event receives one fresh long allocation_key shared by every posting; suppressed events take none. Use primitive sequence Keys_escrow_release, start 3000000000, step 1, reset for this run. AUDIT is dated requested_on; retained funds are due_on, and beneficiary payment is release_on.

Input 0 Source_escrow_1: string contract_id [required]
decimal funding [required]
decimal fee [required]
boolean approved [nullability omitted]
date due_on [required]
date requested_on [required]
date release_on [required]
boolean review [required].
Output 0 Posting_escrow_1: string source_contract_id [required]
string escrow_action [required]
decimal amount [required]
date pay_on [required]
boolean final_payment [required]
long allocation_key [required].
Source contract_id values are unique. Preserve each in source_contract_id on its postings.

```ctl
//#CTL2
string escrow_1_source;
string[] escrow_1_escrow_action_rows = [];
decimal[] escrow_1_amount_rows = [];
date[] escrow_1_pay_on_rows = [];
boolean[] escrow_1_final_payment_rows = [];
long escrow_1_key;
function void stage_escrow_1(string p0, decimal p1, date p2, boolean p3) {
    append(escrow_1_escrow_action_rows, p0);
    append(escrow_1_amount_rows, p1);
    append(escrow_1_pay_on_rows, p2);
    append(escrow_1_final_payment_rows, p3);
}
function integer count() {
    escrow_1_escrow_action_rows = [];
    escrow_1_amount_rows = [];
    escrow_1_pay_on_rows = [];
    escrow_1_final_payment_rows = [];
    escrow_1_source = $in.0.contract_id;
    escrow_1_key = 0L;
    decimal net = $in.0.funding-$in.0.fee;
    /* Branch census:
       1. invalid net funding -> 1 rows
       2. approval unresolved -> 1 rows
       3. approval denied -> 0 rows
       4. not yet due -> 1 rows
       5. reviewed payable release -> 3 rows
       6. ordinary payable release -> 2 rows
    */
    if ($in.0.funding < 0d || $in.0.fee < 0d || net < 0d) {
        escrow_1_key = sequence(Keys_escrow_release, long).next();
        stage_escrow_1("ERROR", 0d, $in.0.requested_on, false);
        return 1; // invalid net funding
    }
    else if ($in.0.approved == null) {
        escrow_1_key = sequence(Keys_escrow_release, long).next();
        stage_escrow_1("PENDING", net, $in.0.requested_on, false);
        return 1; // approval unresolved
    }
    else if ($in.0.approved == false) {
        return 0; // approval denied
    }
    else if ($in.0.requested_on <= $in.0.due_on) {
        escrow_1_key = sequence(Keys_escrow_release, long).next();
        stage_escrow_1("HOLD", net, $in.0.due_on, false);
        return 1; // not yet due
    }
    else if ($in.0.review) {
        escrow_1_key = sequence(Keys_escrow_release, long).next();
        stage_escrow_1("BENEFICIARY", net*(100d-20d)/100d, $in.0.release_on, true);
        stage_escrow_1("AUDIT", 0d, $in.0.requested_on, false);
        stage_escrow_1("RETAIN", net*20d/100d, $in.0.due_on, false);
        return 3; // reviewed payable release
    }
    else if (true) {
        escrow_1_key = sequence(Keys_escrow_release, long).next();
        stage_escrow_1("BENEFICIARY", net, $in.0.release_on, true);
        stage_escrow_1("FEE", $in.0.fee, $in.0.requested_on, false);
        return 2; // ordinary payable release
    }
    return 0;
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.source_contract_id = escrow_1_source;
    $out.0.escrow_action = escrow_1_escrow_action_rows[idx];
    $out.0.amount = escrow_1_amount_rows[idx];
    $out.0.pay_on = escrow_1_pay_on_rows[idx];
    $out.0.final_payment = escrow_1_final_payment_rows[idx];
    $out.0.allocation_key = escrow_1_key;
    return ALL;
}
```

